<title>CANADA: Canada's Prairies to see sunny, warm weather.</title>
<headline>Canada's Prairies to see sunny, warm weather.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's Prairies on Tuesday were forecast to see mainly sunny skies, Environment Canada said.</p>
<p>Alberta should see mainly sunny skies with a few afternoon showers in the north and central regions with highs of 24 to 29 Celsius.</p>
<p>Saskatchewan should see cloud in the west with a chance of rain and sun in the east with highs of 27 to 32 Celsius.</p>
<p>Manitoba should see mainly sunny skies with highs of 25 to 29 Celsius.</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras, Winnipeg Reuters bureau 204 947 3548))</p>
